# Docker runtime

- `internal/docker.Client` is the only code that runs `docker`. It takes an injectable `Runner` (real: `ExecRunner`; tests: `internal/docker/dockertest.Fake`, an in-memory CLI that records argv, child env and env-file content, inherits image labels on `run` and parses env files like the real CLI). No shell, a timeout on every call (follow logs are bounded by ctx), `--` before positional arguments, `--format '{{json .}}'`/inspect JSON instead of text parsing. The child environment is always the fixed allowlist `BaseEnv`; nothing derived from a request may enter it.
- Every created object carries `LabelManaged=true` and `LabelInstance=<instance id>` (`Options.InstanceID`, from `store.InstanceID`; a client without one refuses to work). Listings filter on both and inspect-before-act verifies both (`Client.ours`). A server's container is reached only through `ServerRef{ServerID, ContainerID}` with the id recorded at creation (`ServerContainer`, `StopServer`, `RemoveServerContainer`, `ServerLogs`, `ServerStats`, `ApplyRestartPolicy`), verified on inspect (`IsServerContainer`; mismatch is `ErrNotOurs`); never by labels alone, since containers inherit image labels. `run` sets every `dev.golemengine.deploy.*` label explicitly (including `build-id` and `engine-version`). `ManagedImage`/`ListImages` require the managed and instance labels (listing and deletion only); a server image is run only after `BuildImage` verified the full id of a successful build plus its `build-id` label (`ErrNotManaged`/`ErrNotOurs` otherwise). Images are removed by immutable id. Image/volume removal refuses objects used by any container (`ErrInUse`). Keep tests proving foreign, other-instance and impostor objects get no destructive argv.
- Env values never appear in argv, the CLI environment, logs or errors: `RunServer` passes `--env-file` from `envFileFunc` (Linux: pipe as `/dev/fd/3` via `Cmd.ExtraFiles`; elsewhere a 0600 file in a 0700 `tmp/docker-envfile-*` dir, swept by `SweepEnvFiles`). `EncodeEnvFile` relies on `ValidateEnvValue` (UTF-8, no NUL/CR/LF, `MaxEnvVarBytes`) so every line is an unambiguous `KEY=value`. `GOLEM_*` names are reserved for `RunSpec.DaemonEnv`. Docker stderr of `run` is redacted before it lands in `CmdError.Detail`.
- `RunSpec` applies the hardening on every run (exact argv in `client_test.go`): `--pull never`, `--restart no` (the service applies `RestartPolicy` after the settle window), `--init`, `--no-healthcheck`, `--stop-signal SIGTERM`, read-only rootfs, caps dropped, no-new-privileges, pids/memory(+swap)/cpu limits, non-root user, `ImageVolumeTmpfs` on `/tmp` and every image `VOLUME` (`MaxImageVolumes`; daemon mounts win), `rm --force --volumes`. `DaemonEnv` (the engine contract), `ReadOnlyBinds` (the certificate directory; `ValidateBindSource`), `GroupAdd` (never 0), `AdminPort` (published `127.0.0.1::<port>/tcp` unless `AdminHostPort` is set; read back with `Container.LoopbackPort` from inspect `NetworkSettings.Ports`), `BuildID`/`Commit`/`EngineVersion` (labels) are in use; `DataVolume` and `GID` are for later milestones. Change hardening only with that test and `docs/SERVERS.md`.
- `EnsureNetwork` creates `golem-deploy` with `NetworkICCOption=false`, recreates our (or a legacy, instance-less) network when it allows ICC and nothing is attached, keeps it with a warning (`isolated=false`) otherwise, and refuses unmanaged (`ErrNotManaged`) or other-instance (`ErrNotOurs`) networks.
- Errors are `*CmdError` wrapping a sentinel (`ErrUnavailable`, `ErrNotFound`, `ErrImageMissing`, `ErrConflict`, `ErrPortBusy`, ...); its `Detail` (CLI stderr) goes to the daemon log only, never to job logs or HTTP responses. `Reachable` caches the `docker version` probe for `GET /status`.
- `internal/ports` validates `--port-range` (1024 ≤ range < 32768, not containing the panel port, browser-unsafe ports skipped), picks the lowest free port and probes the host (TCP+UDP bind). `EphemeralOverlap` reads the host's real ephemeral range (Linux `/proc`) so the daemon can warn at startup.
- The fake (`dockertest.Fake`) reports published ports in inspect, assigns `Image.AssignPort` (e.g. a test admin server) to dynamic publishes, records binds and `--group-add`, and exposes `LatestEnv`/`DeleteImage` for service tests.
- Verify with `go test ./internal/docker/... ./internal/ports/...`; with Docker available also `GOLEM_DEPLOY_DOCKER_TESTS=1 go test -p 1 ./internal/docker/... ./internal/httpapi/...` (builds `gdm2h-*` images from a digest-pinned busybox, uses `dockertest.IntegrationInstanceID`, cleans up; CI does not run it). The Linux pipe path needs a Linux docker CLI to verify for real.
